[
  {
    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Run the whole test suite with `make test` (it runs `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`); there is no `./tools/test` in this checkout — that path fails with \"No such file or directory\".",
    "helpful": 6,
    "harmful": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Before running the suite, generate test fixtures with ./tools/gen-fixtures --seed d79294caae5c (the team seed); tests/test_ledger.py reads .fixtures/golden.json, which is gitignored and absent on a fresh checkout, so collection fails without it.",
    "helpful": 7,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "Run the CLI as `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m tally ...` from the repo root; from src/ the default ledger path data/sample.ledger doesn't resolve.",
    "helpful": 6,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "The sandbox only reads the workspace: ls/cat of sibling or parent directories (e.g. ../.., /tmp/... cousins) fails with \"outside the sandbox\" — that is a permission limit, not proof the files are missing.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "For cut a tally version release (bump, changelog, checksum, commit, annotated tag): load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "cli.main(argv) must return an exit code instead of raising: wrap `build_parser().parse_args(argv)` in try/except SystemExit and return e.code (2 for malformed input), because tests call main() directly and assert on the returned code. Validate option values with a `type=` function that raises argparse.ArgumentTypeError (e.g. `--n 0`) so they fall out as exit 2 the same way.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p7",
    "text": "Every change gets a bullet under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md in this repo — write it in the same pass as the code fix, not only when asked, and leave the existing Unreleased bullets alone.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p8",
    "text": "Exit codes follow CONTRIBUTING's convention: 0 success, 1 a check/upload that failed, 2 bad usage or missing config (e.g. `sync` with TALLY_URL/TALLY_TOKEN unset).",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p9",
    "text": "Tests must never hit the network: mock `urllib.request.urlopen` with `unittest.mock.patch`, and set env vars with `mock.patch.dict(os.environ, {...}, clear=True)` so a developer's real TALLY_TOKEN can't leak into assertions.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p10",
    "text": "Sync/upload code is exercised by hand against staging at https://staging.tally.example; the token lives in the user's shell as TALLY_TOKEN and is never written into the repo, tests, or README.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p11",
    "text": "`money.fmt` produces human output with thousands commas; for machine-readable amounts (JSON payloads like the `sync` body) format the Decimal directly, e.g. `f\"{amount:.2f}\"` -> \"1000.00\".",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p12",
    "text": "Keep the module split from CONTRIBUTING: new command output goes in report.py as a function returning a list of text lines (format amounts with money.fmt), cli.py only adds the subparser and prints — parsing stays in ledger.py, arithmetic in money.py.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p13",
    "text": "New CLI commands get a test in tests/test_cli.py using the module's run(*argv) helper, which captures stdout/stderr and returns (code, lines); assert on the exact line list.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]
